Subject: alt.extropians: proposed FAQ outline

Since the newsgroup has been created, perhaps we can capitalize on it.
Below I offer a tentative FAQ outline to be posted to the group, in 
order to suggest basic topics for discussion.  Also note that I haven't 
mentioned the existence of an Extropian mailing list, but I have
mentioned several organizations which will benefit from inquiries and
orders (eg, ExI).  Given a plethora of topics from which to choose, and
a moderate reading list, readers of the newsgroup can be exposed to basic
extropian memes (winning converts) and kept busy (ie, avoiding a sudden
rush to join this list).  Since the list is brand new, now would be a
great time to exploit the opportunity to expose new subscribers to these
ideas, that is, while they're making the decision on whether or not to
subscribe regularly.  There are a few areas that, while attractive to
many extropians, are potentially going to be misunderstood by new prospects,
eg, "anarchy", "anything-goes unbreakable cryptography", "immortality", 
"weapons stockpiling", etc., so wherever possible I've tried to tone it
down and avoid sensitive wording.  Comments on this overall strategy?

Note -- Since I'm still a newbie, I'm in a position to profit
from reading discussions and debates of the basics, and perhaps now 
and then to contribute to it.  If someone's gotta do it, it might 
as well be me :-)

Below is my proposed post to the newsgroup.  Comments on the outline?

----------------------------------------------------------------------

